course: dictionary
lesson: 7383
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Plum is a fruit, a colour, and a word for a very good job. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «The cake had flour, water, currants, plums and sugar in it.» Plums here are fruit, because you bake them and eat them. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Her scarf was a deep plum colour.» Here plum is a colour, because you can be a colour but not a fruit. «She got a plum job at the museum» means a very good job. Try each meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: A plum is a small round soft fruit with a smooth skin and a stone inside.
fact: Plums can have purple, red or yellow skins.
fact: The stone inside a plum is its seed.
fact: Dried plums are called prunes.
fact: «Plum» can also mean a dark red-purple colour, or a very good job.
exercise: «There are 15 plums in a bowl.» What is the stone inside a plum? | Its leaf | Its skin | Its juice | *Its seed
exercise: «The wall was painted a deep plum.» What does plum mean here? | A type of bird | *A dark red-purple colour | A very good job | A small round fruit
exercise: «She got a plum job at the bank.» What does plum mean here? | A dark red-purple colour | *A very good job | A bowl of fruit | A small round fruit
test: What are dried plums called? | *Prunes | Raisins | Currants | Figs
test: In «He made one cake with flour, water, currants, plums and sugar», what are the plums? | *Fruit to eat | A colour | A kind of tree | A job
exam: Which meaning fits «She wore a plum scarf to school»? | A very good job | *A dark red-purple colour | A type of cake | A small round fruit
